.env
.venv*/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.playwright*/

# Regenerable review output. scripts/tapstitch_preview.py rebuilds the whole
# sheet in about seven minutes, and it is rebuilt on every spacing change, so
# committing ~6MB of PNGs each time would bloat history for no gain. The
# published artifact is the shareable copy.
artifacts/tapstitch-previews/

# Regenerable print output, same reasoning as the proof sheet. The three front
# logo files are rebuilt by every tapstitch_build.py run, and the 135 back print
# files are not here at all: they are written into each temple's own folder under
# Temples/, which is outside this repo. Committing one half of a generated pair
# would be worse than committing neither.
artifacts/tapstitch/front-logo/

# Captured Tapstitch editor traffic. Recorded by scripts/tapstitch_capture.py to
# work out how the editor saves a design. Redacted at capture time, but a body
# can still carry account detail, so it never goes in git.
artifacts/tapstitch/network/

# On-model photo mockup spike. The PNG originals of the base and colourway
# photos are 96MB; artifacts/photo-mockup-spike/source-photos/ holds the same 19
# images as quality-95 JPEG at 15MB, which is the recoverable copy. The PNGs
# stay on disk (this workspace is in iCloud) but do not belong in history, for
# the same reason the proof sheet and print files above do not.
artifacts/photo-mockup-spike/bases/
artifacts/photo-mockup-spike/colourway-photos/
artifacts/photo-mockup-spike/model_blank.png

# Rebuilt from source-photos plus composite_set.py in about 16 seconds.
artifacts/photo-mockup-spike/final-set/

# Re-downloadable from Tapstitch. STATE.md records the URL scheme: the version
# number in a Tapstitch filename is a unix timestamp and the folder it sits in
# is that timestamp's date, which recovers any asset from its filename alone.
artifacts/photo-mockup-spike/tapstitch-on-model/
